# Android SDK location (required). Android Studio sets this automatically.
sdk.dir=/path/to/android-sdk

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no service URL to configure.
#
# This file used to document EARSLATE_WORKER_URL, pointing at a session broker
# on api.classeve.com. That broker was removed in 0.4.0 and its route now 404s:
# earslate mints session credentials on-device from the user's own provider key
# and has no backend of any kind. A debug build needs nothing here but sdk.dir.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Release signing: two keys, because the APK and the AAB go to different places.
#
# The APK is the direct download. It is signed with the brand key, set by the
# four EARSLATE_* properties, whose DN must be `CN=Earslate, O=ClassEve, C=IN`
# and nothing else: `verifyReleaseIdentity` runs after every assembleRelease and
# fails the build on any other DN, or on entity strings in the APK's bytes.
#
# The AAB goes to Google Play, which accepts only the upload certificate it
# registered for this app. It is signed with the upload key, set by the four
# PLAY_UPLOAD_* properties; `verifyBundleIdentity` checks the certificate's
# SHA-256 against the pin in app/build.gradle.kts.
#
# There is no debug fallback: `verifyReleaseSigning` fails a release build when
# a property is missing or the keystore file does not exist.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EARSLATE_STORE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/brand.keystore
# EARSLATE_STORE_PASSWORD=...
# EARSLATE_KEY_ALIAS=...
# EARSLATE_KEY_PASSWORD=...
#
# PLAY_UPLOAD_STORE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/upload.keystore
# PLAY_UPLOAD_STORE_PASSWORD=...
# PLAY_UPLOAD_KEY_ALIAS=...
# PLAY_UPLOAD_KEY_PASSWORD=...
#
# Strings no release artifact may contain, base64 and comma-separated. A release
# build fails without them; the gates scan every APK and AAB for each one.
# EARSLATE_IDENTITY_NEEDLES=...
